# Repo-root .dockerignore — the build context for BOTH images is the repo root
# (see deploy/Dockerfile.api / deploy/Dockerfile.web). Docker only reads
# `.dockerignore` from the context root or `<dockerfile>.dockerignore`; a file
# under deploy/ is silently ignored. Keep the context small and never ship
# local state or secrets.
**/.venv
**/venv
**/node_modules
**/.next
**/.turbo
**/.git
**/.github
**/.ruff_cache
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/.pytest_cache
**/.mypy_cache
**/*.tsbuildinfo
**/*.db
**/test_*.db
**/*.log
**/coverage
**/.coverage
**/.DS_Store
# Never ship env files; the example files are safe (no real values).
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
# Docs / diagrams are not needed at runtime.
docs/diagrams/rendered
